secubox-meshtastic (0.1.6-1~bookworm1) bookworm; urgency=medium

  * Device config view: new GET /api/v1/meshtastic/device-config returns the
    RAK's live configuration read from the radio — firmware, hw model, node
    id/name, region, modem preset, hop limit, TX enabled, role, Bluetooth
    (enabled + pairing mode + fixed PIN), WiFi, channels — with all protobuf
    enums decoded to names (EU_868 / LONG_FAST / RAK4631 / CLIENT / FIXED_PIN).
    Panel: a "Config du device" section on the Grid tab. Read-only, JWT-gated.
    (This is also where the phone-pairing Bluetooth PIN is now visible.)
  * Harden the intermittent restart crash: uvicorn os.remove(uds) on a stale
    foreign-owned socket in the 1777-sticky /run/secubox raised PermissionError
    and killed the daemon. main() now clears its own stale socket before
    uvicorn binds (ExecStartPre=+/bin/rm still covers the foreign case).
    Verified: two back-to-back restarts, NRestarts=0, zero socket errors.

 -- Gerald KERMA <devel@cybermind.fr>  Wed, 29 Jul 2026 08:45:00 +0200

